# Normalise line endings to LF in the repo and the working copy regardless
# of platform. This stops Windows clones from showing phantom "modified"
# files in GitHub Desktop whenever a tool rewrites a file — git was
# (silently) wanting to convert LF to CRLF on checkout because of the
# `core.autocrlf=true` default on Windows.
#
# `text=auto` lets git detect text files; `eol=lf` pins the line ending
# in the working copy. CI (Linux) and Windows devs now see the same
# file contents byte-for-byte.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary file types — git should never try to normalise these.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.webp  binary
*.svg   binary
*.ico   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.docx  binary
*.xlsx  binary
*.pptx  binary
*.zip   binary
*.gz    binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.eot   binary
